siglip2-b16-224-tokenizer-c58ce867.json         (converted)
  Model:    SigLIP 2, Google
  Upstream: https://huggingface.co/google/siglip2-base-patch16-224
            revision 75de2d55ec2d0b4efc50b3e9ad70dba96a7b2fa2
  License:  Apache-2.0
  Changes:  vision and text towers exported from PyTorch to ONNX (opset 17)
            with L2-normalized embedding outputs; the vision tower is FP32;
            the text tower's token-embedding table is taken out of the graph
            and stored as int8 with a float32 per-row scale (the two .npy
            files); the tokenizer is the model's own tokenizer.json with
            lowercasing, padding and truncation to 64 tokens added.
  Data:     trained by Google on the WebLI dataset, which is not public.

rtdetr-r18-o365-a8b2b37f.onnx  (converted; superseded)
  Model:    RT-DETR-R18. Code: https://github.com/lyuwenyu/RT-DETR
  Upstream: https://huggingface.co/PekingU/rtdetr_r18vd_coco_o365
            revision 386c43855d01bcd966e548f3296fbd2cd2a2a40b
  License:  Apache-2.0 (code and published weights)
  Changes:  exported to ONNX (opset 16, 640x640, FP32) with the same merged
            [1, 300, 84] output as rtdetr-v2-r18-coco above.
  Data:     pretrained on Objects365, then fine-tuned on COCO 2017. The
            Objects365 publisher makes that dataset available for academic
            purposes only (https://www.objects365.org/download.html), so this
            file should not be assumed to be cleared for commercial use.
            VS-NVR no longer ships it; it stays only so that older VS-NVR
            source revisions, which pin it by hash, can still be built.
